# Wave W17-V (Heritage Forest): manor oak — an ancient spread-crowned oak in deep manor greens, its canopy wider than any road tree in the fleet, coin-light highlight lifted clear of the shade turf, on deep turf (ground baked in). The forest’s own tree — split from Route 202’s mature approach oak by the spread and the darkness (a garden avenue tree vs a forest elder) and from Maris’s silk oak by register: the manor oak shades a ballroom, the silk oak a bright wood.
